Fix DevStyle's base stylesheet being rejected by the Eclipse 2026-09 (4.41)
CSS parser once its imports resolve (see 0001 for the import side).

DevStyle serves its CSS through the devstyle: URL handler, whose generator
drops whole lines carrying theme/OS markers such as /*LIGHTONLY*/ or
/*MACONLY*/ before the engine parses the result. One block in
globalstyle.css carries the marker on its opening selector line but not on
its closing brace, so every dark theme is served a stray declaration plus a
lone "}" at top level. The SAC-based parser up to 4.40 recovered from that
silently; the strict in-house parser of 4.41 throws CssParseException
("Expected IDENT but found WS"), the ThemeEngine does not catch runtime
exceptions from a stylesheet, and the theme restore aborts — on startup that
means "An error has occurred" again (revstyle issue #7). Verified by running
the 4.41 parser over the generator's output for every dark/light x
linux/win32/macosx combination: this is the only rejected construct.

Mark the entire block light-only. Light themes receive exactly the text they
always did; dark themes now receive nothing here instead of junk, which is
also what the old parser effectively made of it. (Removing the marker from
the selector line would instead give dark themes the #202425 background the
block seems to have wanted for the MyEclipse dashboard; this repo prefers
the behaviour-preserving change.)

Target: com.genuitec.eclipse.theming.css 2025.2.0.202509301431 (resource
patch — the file is repacked from work/, no compilation involved)
Context source: the bundle's own css/include/globalstyle.css.
Details: docs/css-parser-strictness.md

--- a/com.genuitec.eclipse.theming.css/css/include/globalstyle.css
+++ b/com.genuitec.eclipse.theming.css/css/include/globalstyle.css
@@ -427,10 +427,12 @@
     swt-unselected-hot-tab-color-background: #161616; /* Bug 465711 */
 }
 
+/* revstyle: the whole block is light-only. The opening line always was, so dark
+   themes used to receive a stray declaration and brace here; the SAC parser of
+   Eclipse <= 4.40 skipped them, the strict parser of 4.41 aborts the stylesheet. */
 #myeclipse-dashboard-body Composite{ /*LIGHTONLY*/
-	background-color: #202425; /*DARKONLY*/
     background-color: #010101; /*LIGHTONLY*/
-}
+} /*LIGHTONLY*/
 
 #myeclipse-dashboard-body Label{/*LIGHTONLY*/
     background-color: #010101; /*LIGHTONLY*/
